Original commit body from 8f5fa8d1ec231070e34876c734d1e3d5941adbce:

try_analyze_with_rust_analyzer returned a bare Optional[Tuple], and its
None collapsed four states the exception taxonomy already told apart: a
missing binary, a non-zero exit, an exit-0-with-no-index, and an
undecodable SCIP blob. The analyzer filed all four as
"rust-analyzer backend produced no output" with skip_reason_code
"unreported", so a user could not tell "install rust-analyzer" from
"your workspace is not a cargo project" from "the indexer crashed".

ScipAttempt carries the verdict out of the boundary:

  missing binary         -> dependency_unavailable
  non-zero exit/timeout  -> pass_crashed
  undecodable SCIP index -> pass_crashed
  exit 0, no index       -> unreported

pass_crashed follows ADR-0056's init-failure ruling, which put caught
constructor exceptions there on the grounds that the value says nothing
about WHO contained the raise. The exit-0-with-no-index case keeps the
declared residue on purpose: it is not a crash and not a missing
dependency, and the axis has no value for "an enabled backend completed
without producing anything to read". Inventing a neighbour would be a
fabricated disclosure, so the gap is documented in ScipAttempt rather
than filled.

A backend that RAN TO COMPLETION and indexed nothing is no longer a skip
at all. It returns a real AnalysisRun with
silence_reason=no_candidate_construct, claimed by the body. Falling
through to derive_silence_reason would have stamped no_candidate_files
-- "received zero input files, and no mechanism would change it" -- on a
repository that may be full of .rs, which is the exact false assertion
ADR-0056 W3 was built to stop, one pass to the left.

The skip-hosted values stay skip-hosted. Re-hosting
dependency_unavailable and pass_crashed onto an AnalysisRun is the
question ADR-0056 item 5 reserves to the owner; discriminating the
states does not pre-empt that ruling.

Live repro on a non-cargo repo with the backend enabled:
  before {"reason": "rust-analyzer backend produced no output",
          "skip_reason_code": "unreported"}
  after  {"reason": "rust-analyzer backend: rust-analyzer scip exited 1",
          "skip_reason_code": "pass_crashed"}

Five pre-existing tests and one assertion pinning the conflated prose
string were re-pointed rather than deleted.

Closes WI-luvud

